.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt PROCMON 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm procmon
.Nd inspect native FreeBSD system calls with DTrace
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl p Ar pid Ns Oo ,pid... Oc
.Op Fl e Ar syscall Ns Oo ,syscall... Oc
.Op Fl c Op Ar file
.Op Fl -duration-ms Ar milliseconds
.Nm
.Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl -dump
.Op Fl p Ar pids
.Op Fl e Ar syscalls
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This community port of Microsoft ProcMon-Linux uses the native
.Fx
ELF64
syscall provider, base DTrace/CTF, ELF symbols, curses and SQLite.
The validated target is
.Fx
15.1 amd64.
Live capture requires tracing privileges and an available syscall provider.
The application does not load modules or change boot, privilege or sysctl
policy.
.Pp
By default, all available native syscall schemas and native user processes
except the monitor are selected.
PID selection binds capture to inspected process identities.
Capture stops when every selected process exits.
Exec changes the selected image and ends identity-scoped capture as a failure.
Children are not automatically added.
.Pp
Without
.Fl c
or
.Fl -dump ,
an interactive terminal of at least 80 columns by 24 rows is required.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--duration-ms milliseconds"
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display usage without starting tracing.
.It Fl -version
Display the port version.
.It Fl p , Fl -pids Ar list
Select up to ten comma-separated native ELF64 PIDs.
.Fl -pid
is an alias.
.It Fl e , Fl -events Ar list
Select comma-separated native syscall names.
.It Fl -list-events
List available native names and argument types; requires tracing privileges.
.It Fl c , Fl -collect Op Ar file
Capture without curses and save a new
.Fx
SQLite trace.
The default filename is
.Pa procmon_<epoch>.db .
An existing destination is rejected.
.It Fl f , Fl -file Ar file
Replay a
.Fx
trace without opening DTrace.
Only file read access is needed.
.It Fl -dump
With
.Fl f ,
write typed JSON Lines instead of displaying curses.
.It Fl -duration-ms Ar milliseconds
Stop live capture after 1 through 86400000 milliseconds from readiness.
Pause time counts toward this wall-clock limit.
.It Fl -max-events Ar count
Live event budget, 1 through 1000000; default 100000.
.It Fl -max-bytes Ar count
Live encoded/display payload budget, 1 through 268435456; default 67108864.
This is not a total resident-memory limit.
.It Fl -no-strings
Disable selected bounded pathname snapshots; retain pointer values.
.It Fl -no-buffers
Disable selected bounded input/output buffer snapshots.
.It Fl -no-stacks
Disable user-stack capture and symbol work.
.It Fl l , Fl -log Ar file
Write a debug log.
.It Fl s , Fl -storageEngine Cm sql
Select the supported SQLite engine.
.El
.Sh INTERACTIVE KEYS
Arrow/page keys navigate events.
Enter opens/closes event details; arrow/page keys scroll details.
F1 shows help, F2 sorting, F3 search, F4 filtering, F5 pause/resume,
F6 export and F8 statistics.
Use q or F9 to quit.
Save with F6 before quitting; repeated exports use numbered new paths.
.Sh TRACE DATA
All metadata argument positions are retained as exact 64-bit lanes, up to eight.
Selected paths are bounded to 256 bytes, selected buffers to 32 bytes and user
stacks to 16 PCs.
A limit flag also covers a value exactly as long as its bound.
Pointed-to structures, iovecs and argv/envp are not recursively decoded.
ELF symbols are best effort and unavailable values are marked.
.Pp
Timestamps are relative to DTrace BEGIN, in nanoseconds in storage/JSON.
Displayed durations are milliseconds.
The UTC start label is not an exact conversion of the DTrace clock.
Errno, result, evidence and completed, restart, control-transfer, entry-only,
cancelled and incomplete states are separate fields.
.Pp
Files are private, mode 0600.
.Fx
traces carry a separate platform/version identifier; Linux files are
rejected.
Replay validates typed rows and their query columns before loading, with a
256 MiB payload budget.
JSON strings map bytes to codepoints; Latin-1 encoding recovers original bytes.
Consumers must retain exact 64-bit integers.
.Sh SIGNALS AND FAILURES
SIGINT and SIGTERM stop and drain tracing, without terminating targets.
Headless mode exports retained data before returning.
Faults, drops, missing snapshots, unresolved pairs, pause gaps, target changes
and stop reason are recorded in metadata.
Budget exhaustion fails explicitly; a failed transaction is rolled back.
A partial capture is not proof that every call or byte was observed.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "130, 143"
.It 0
Success; inspect metadata for cancellation or pause gaps.
.It 1
Capture, quality, target, storage or terminal failure.
.It 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.It 130, 143
SIGINT or SIGTERM stop, respectively.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Replace 1234 with a live native process PID:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
doas procmon -p 1234
doas procmon -p 1234 -e openat,read,write -c capture.db
doas procmon -f capture.db
doas procmon -f capture.db --dump > capture.jsonl
.Ed
.Sh LIMITATIONS
The validated release/architecture is
.Fx
15.1 amd64.
Runtime tests select owned fixture PIDs.
Unfiltered unrelated workloads, sustained production load, jails, other releases
and ABIs, and Linux runtime regression have not been validated.
DTrace syscall probes and kernel CTF fields are private interfaces.
There is no kernel-stack or source-line view.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtrace 1 ,
.Xr procstat 1
